#!ipxe
echo Mode: windows
echo Booting Windows from local disk...
echo
# Exit with a different code or use sanboot to target the Windows drive
# For now, we rely on BIOS boot order: if PXE exits, BIOS tries the next device.
# Set Windows NVMe as the second boot device in BIOS for this to work.
#
# If both NVMe drives are in the boot order, we need to control which one
# boots. Options:
#   1. sanboot --drive 0x80  (first BIOS drive — typically Windows)
#   2. chain specific EFI path on the Windows ESP
#
# This will need tuning after first boot — see docs for details.
exit 0
